// Clinic notes
/obj/item/paper/fluff/formaldehyde
	name = "formaldehyde memo"
	default_raw_text = {"<h2><center><b>Regarding Formaldehyde</b></center></h2>
	<hr>
	After a long time of begging the city, they've agreed to give us funding to purchase medical formaldehyde.
	However, they were very clear that we were <b>NOT</b> to waste it. Consider this note a guide, unless you want to talk
	to someone who can do more than just write a note.
	<hr>
	<h3>\"Section A.: My patient was deceased when they arrived!\"</h3><br>
	● Take an eyedropper from the storage room (if your coworkers aren't savages, there will be a few on the table where you found this note).<br>
	● Draw 1 unit of formaldehyde from the bottle on the table with this note (once again, assuming your coworkers aren't savages).<br>
	● Apply the solution into the open eye of the cadaver. This will prevent decay of the cadaver's organs.<br>
	● Mend the wounds of the patient as much as possible.<br>
	● Perform neurosurgery.<br>
	● Perform a coronary bypass <b>ONLY IF NEEDED</b>.<br>
	● Perform lobectomy <b>ONLY IF NEEDED</b>.<br>
	● Perform a hepatectomy <b>ONLY IF NEEDED</b>.<br>
	● Perform a gastrectomy <b>ONLY IF NEEDED</b>.<br>
	● Make sure they have enough blood to sustain respiration.<br>
	● Apply shock.<br>
	● Perform CPR <b>OR</b> treat with 2 to 5 units of convermol (or 5 units of salbutomol).<br>
	● When respirtory distress subsides, apply anesthetic mask.<br>
	● Continue surgery until patient is stable.<br>
	● Success! You've saved a life!<br>
	<hr>
	<h3>\"Section B.: We're all out of formaldehyde!\"</h3><br>
	● Are you sure? Check the morgue.<br>
	● Extend the injection tube from the tank into your bottle.<br>
	<hr>
	<h3>\"Section C.: The patient's organ has already been treated!\"</h3><br>
	● Don't panic. Obtain a replacement organ from storage. The freezer should be in the corner of this room (we're assuming things again).<br>
	<hr>
	<h3>\"Section D.: There are no more organs in storage!\"</h3><br>
	● Follow steps 1-5 of section A.<br>
	● File an organ transplant form (FFr-99b)<br>
	● <del>Keep the body frozen for up to 4 hours and no more.</del><br>
	<h6><font color=\"#708090\">There are other ways. None that I can write down with the director watching. Be smart. See the <del>dealer</del>.</font><h6>
	"}
